Warrick,<br />
<br />
You asked for everything the Division of Examinations holds on Ottoway Tras=
k examination 2012-0331. Here it is, and it is short.<br />
<br />
SENTRY holds a summary record and one scanned letter. The summary record gi=
ves the registrant, fieldwork dates of April 16 to May 4, 2012, the examine=
r in charge, and disposition code C-1, closed with no deficiencies. The sca=
nned letter is the closing letter of August 9, 2012, three paragraphs, stat=
ing that the staff has completed the examination and noted no deficiencies.=
<br />
<br />
I want to be careful about two different things here.<br />
<br />
First, the migration caveat applies to this examination as it applies to ev=
ery pre-2014 examination in this office - correspondence and work papers we=
re out of scope in 2016 and are not in SENTRY. So the thinness of the file =
is not by itself evidence about what happened.<br />
<br />
Second, and this cuts the other way, the disposition code we hold is C-1 an=
d not C-2. C-1 was the legacy code for closed with no deficiencies. C-2 was=
 closed with no further action. If an undertaking had been obtained the cod=
e should have been C-4, and I know from Marcus's extract that C-4 records w=
ere rewritten to C-2 at cutover, not to C-1. A C-1 is a positive statement =
that the examiners found nothing, and it is not the code the mapping proble=
m produces.<br />
<br />
I am told Count II was pleaded off a line in the 2013 branch tracking sprea=
dsheet. I have that spreadsheet. The line reads "OTA - undertaking obtained=
, follow up next cycle." It is one cell of free text in a document that als=
o has three rows for registrants this office never examined.<br />
